A Russian Baltic Fleet corvette was hit by multiple Ukrainian drones during a large attack on the Ust-Luga port, a senior Estonian military officer said Friday.
Speaking at the regular Friday Ministry of Defense briefing, deputy commander of the Estonian Defense Forces (EDF) division Col. Aron Kalmus said deaths and injuries resulted from the strike, on the Naro-Fominsk, a Sviyazhsk-class corvette.
The vessel was damaged and could not continue under its own power, requiring escort toward St Petersburg by another vessel. The incident follows Wednesday's pre-dawn drone alert across eight Estonian counties, a scramble of NATO fighters, and fires at the Russian port of Ust-Luga being visible from eastern Estonia.
